<title>USA: Emery, USAir, Northwest in US defence bid.</title>
<headline>Emery, USAir, Northwest in US defence bid.</headline>
<dateline>REDWOOD CITY, California 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Emery Worldwide said the U.S. Defense Department has renewed a $22.5 million contract for an Emery-led consortium of air carriers to carry freight for the U.S. Air Mobility Command.</p>
<p>Other consortium members include USAir and Northwest Airlines, Emery said in a statement.</p>
<p>Consortium members transport equipment and supplies from the United States to U.S. Army locations in Germany, Italy and Japan.</p>
<p>Consignments include express shipment of medical products to the U.S. Armed Forces headquarters in Germany for redistribution to U.S. Army installations throughout Europe, said Emery.</p>
<p>Roughly 75,000 pounds a month of medical products are moved by the consortium.</p>
<p>-Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
